{
  "id": "ep150",
  "duration": 58.376,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.804,
      "text": "Astronomers first saw a faint violet speck, calling it an ordinary star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Camara schmidt tonantzintla.jpg",
        "credit": "Gsrdzl",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camara_schmidt_tonantzintla.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.8,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.804,
      "end": 15.074,
      "text": "In 1957, Mexican astronomers catalogued it as entry 618, unaware of the monster lurking 10.8 billion light-years away.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 15.067,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.074,
      "end": 23.344,
      "text": "This point of light is an ultramassive black hole with an event horizon radius of 1,300 astronomical units.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Artist\u2019s impression of quasar J0313-1806.jpg",
        "credit": "NOIRLab/NSF/AURA/J. da Silva",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_quasar_J0313-1806.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.067,
          "end": 20.333,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 20.333,
          "end": 23.333,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.344,
      "end": 28.989,
      "text": "That is 40 times Pluto\u2019s distance from the Sun, all contained within one dark sphere.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.333,
          "end": 29.0,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.989,
      "end": 37.184,
      "text": "Gas whipping around the void at 10,000 kilometers per second fuels a brilliance equal to 140 trillion Suns.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Supermassive black hole.tif",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Supermassive_black_hole.tif"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 29.0,
          "end": 32.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 32.1,
          "end": 37.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.184,
      "end": 44.629,
      "text": "Initial measurements found 66 billion solar masses, later revised to 40.7 billion Suns.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Meyers b15 s0117a.jpg",
        "credit": "various",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meyers_b15_s0117a.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.2,
          "end": 44.633,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.629,
      "end": 53.354,
      "text": "Wrapped in a glowing hydrogen nebula over 300,000 light-years across, it remains one of the heaviest objects in existence.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 44.633,
          "end": 53.367,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 53.354,
      "end": 58.026,
      "text": "No monster in the cosmos has ever hidden behind such a quiet disguise.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Camara schmidt tonantzintla.jpg",
        "credit": "Gsrdzl",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Camara_schmidt_tonantzintla.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 53.367,
          "end": 58.367,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
